# The direct dependencies of the backend. Change this file, not requirements.txt.
#
# requirements.txt is the lock file: every package with an exact version and its hashes. CI, the
# Docker image and Render install from it, so they get the versions that the tests checked.
# Make it again after a change here (from the backend/ folder):
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt --generate-hashes --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --python-version 3.15
#
# The platform and the Python version are the ones of the production image (backend/Dockerfile).
# Without -U, uv keeps the versions that are already in requirements.txt. Add -U, or -P <package>
# for one package, to move to newer versions. See docs/deployment.md, "Backend dependencies".
